aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P2 (S2): "infinite" is taken as goodness unlimited in perfection as God's nature, which does not require that everything be good in P2 and as goodness unbounded in extent, filling everything so no contrary remains where infinite_goodness is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S3) does not follow (aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r2.sense1)
aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C1 (S3): evil_exists = T, god_exists = T, infinite_goodness = F, infinite_goodness_2 = T
